= Confidence rationale =

[[Has type::Text]]

A concise explanation of why the present evidence justifies the current level of reliance on a claim, including material support, limitations, contradictory evidence, scope, and what would change the assessment.

This property is preferred over arbitrary universal numerical confidence scores.

Quantitative probability/confidence may still be recorded elsewhere when a domain supplies a meaningful calibration model.

See [[BITwiki:Epistemics]] and [[BITwiki:Claim validation]].
